one-county"],["ARC or PLC in Limestone County","/arc-plc/texas/limestone-county"],["PRF calculator","/prf"]],"story":"<p class=\"prf-lede prf-story\">As of Oct 12, the record here runs 75 years, 1951 to 2025, on the middle value of the county&rsquo;s 11 grids. July to August is the driest pair with a normal of 4.21 inches, and it came in under 90% of normal in 39 of those years. In 2025 June to July ran 177% of normal on the middle, then November to December 2025 fell to 48%. So far in 2026, February to March sits at 34% of normal on the middle.</p>"}
